{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Both issues resolved, and the second one turned out to be a real bug worth reporting.\n\n**The inspect script works now** — it's at `/tmp/cledger-inspect.py` (my earlier write landed somewhere your shell couldn't see; this one is written through the shell, so it's really there):\n\n```sh\ncd /tmp/octest2 && cledger log --json | python3 /tmp/cledger-inspect.py\n```\n\nThat's your original TUI session, re-captured from opencode's DB into a fresh repo at `/tmp/octest2` — identical 8 events with identical seqs, even though `/tmp/octest` is gone. Side benefit: that's a live demonstration that event ids are content-derived and repo-independent, and that a session outlives the directory it ran in.\n\n**The bug you hit is real and pre-existing.** `printJsonl` is untouched by this branch and identical in `main`. It writes to `process.stdout` with no `error` handler, so when the reader goes away mid-write, Node throws an unhandled `EPIPE` and dumps a stack trace instead of exiting quietly. I characterized exactly when it fires:\n\n- Reader dies before cledger writes (`cledger log --json | python3 /nonexistent.py`) — **crashes**\n- `cledger export | head -1` on your real 23MB ledger — **crashes**\n- `| head -2` on a small 13KB ledger — fine, because it all fits in the 64KB pipe buffer\n\nSo it's not exotic: `cledger export | head` on any real-sized ledger hits it. It affects `log --json`, `show --json`, and `export` — all three go through `printJsonl`.\n\nThe fix is small — an `EPIPE` handler on stdout, exiting 0 the way `head`-friendly CLIs do. I've left it alone because this PR is about the opencode adapter and mixing an unrelated CLI fix in would muddy review. Want me to do it as a separate branch/PR, or fold it into #2?\n\nHousekeeping: `/tmp/octest2` is still around if you want to poke at it further; `rm -rf /tmp/octest2` when done. The probe files (`~/.config/opencode/plugin/_probe.js`, `~/opencode-events.jsonl`) are also still present if the cleanup you ran only covered `/tmp/octest`.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"c70ed9d897dd2ec353154a754a100bd72c311c79","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":616},"id":"ev1-8d991fee9f86b05b2ded9a8bbb67dc48a7e6fcf3db5823ab482b98b641d6b625","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-03T03:22:29.445Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Both issues resolved, and the second one turned out to be a real bug worth reporting.\n\n**The inspect script works now** — it's at `/tmp/cledger-inspect.py` (my earlier write landed somewhere your shell couldn't see; this one is written through the shell, so it's really there):\n\n```sh\ncd /tmp/octest2 && cledger log --json | python3 /tmp/cledger-inspect.py\n```\n\nThat's your original TUI session, re-captured from opencode's DB into a fresh repo at `/tmp/octest2` — identical 8 events with identical seqs, even though `/tmp/octest` is gone. Side benefit: that's a live demonstration that event ids are content-derived and repo-independent, and that a session outlives the directory it ran in.\n\n**The bug you hit is real and pre-existing.** `printJsonl` is untouched by this branch and identical in `main`. It writes to `process.stdout` with no `error` handler, so when the reader goes away mid-write, Node throws an unhandled `EPIPE` and dumps a stack trace i